Hi Daniel, thank you again for the detailed explanations and warnings! It all makes sense. At the moment I'm making some coding & numerical explorations of Nimble, some of which don't make much sense probabilistically, just to understand correctly how Nimble works, so that I won't misuse it.

I've indeed noticed that if an end node contains data, then Nimble does not use a posterior_predictive sampler, but a more general MCMC sampler (except in special situations such as conjugacy, very smart!).

Thank you very much again,
